WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.027
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.077 --> 00:00:05.740
Junior Makers, video 6.

3
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.340
Sensors: notice light, touch, distance.

4
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:16.030
Sensors turn something in the world into a signal a circuit can use.

5
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.555
A light sensor can turn on a night lamp in the dark.

6
00:00:21.605 --> 00:00:24.582
A button can start a doorbell buzzer.

7
00:00:24.632 --> 00:00:29.000
A distance sensor can help a robot slow before a wall.

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:37.383
In Robotics 101 you will wire infrared sensors and motors on a real line-follower.

9
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:42.480
This course builds the vocabulary first: sense, think, act.

10
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.388
Let us recap.

11
00:00:45.438 --> 00:00:48.708
Sensors notice; actuators act.

12
00:00:48.758 --> 00:00:52.691
Pair a sensor with a clear reaction.

13
00:00:52.741 --> 00:00:55.900
Next: Plan: who does it help?
